  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_1",
  "label": "Alcohol consumption consequence mapped to dehumanized Black woman",
  "description": "The text 'too much alcohol' is mapped onto the visual of the hand holding the beer can, while the text 'end result' is mapped onto the visual of the Black woman with darkened skin and stern expression. This creates an analogical mapping where the visual of the woman is projected as the consequence of excessive alcohol consumption, invoking a harmful racial stereotype that equates Black people with primates or animals. The mapping is explicit through the juxtaposition and labeling, where the woman's appearance is used to represent the 'end result' of drinking, thus linking the textual concept of alcohol consequence to the visual representation of a dehumanized Black person.",
